    { math: '1 · The classic pipeline', note: 'Lexers and parsers (the compilers lesson\'s grammar machinery) → part-of-speech tagging → named entities → parsing trees → meaning representation. Rule-based NLP (1960s–1990) was hand-built and brittle.' },
    { math: '2 · Statistical NLP (1990→)', note: 'Let probabilities do the work: learn patterns from millions of examples. Machine translation improved dramatically when IBM\'s models (Brown et al., 1990) fed on parallel texts — "every time I fire a linguist, performance goes up" (a quoted half-truth at IBM).' },
